WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.847
Percent means per hundred, so thirty five percent shades thirty five of these hundred equal cells

00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:09.668
The percentage alone is a relative amount

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:14.100
Its actual size depends on the whole to which it refers.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.869
To find thirty five percent of sixty, multiply the whole sixty by the fraction thirty five hundredths

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:23.772
The result is twenty one

00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:29.100
Keep track of which quantity is the whole and which quantity is the part.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.361
A twenty five percent increase keeps the original whole and adds a quarter of it

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:41.526
The combined factor is one point two five, taking sixty to seventy five

00:00:41.526 --> 00:00:45.500
This factor form makes repeated percentage changes easier to track.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:55.226
Dropping from seventy five back to sixty is a twenty percent decrease, because the new comparison whole is seventy five

00:00:55.226 --> 00:01:01.967
Equal absolute changes can have different percentages; always name the starting amount used as the denominator.
